 Preserve the original normal parser result;do not add an alphanumeric check
 absent from this branch. Source-derived managed normal-parser/browser evidence,
 not a full outer LanguageTag validity or native execution claim. Task196.
+
+## CALC-184 — short numeric-region Locale depends on registry initialization order
+
+Source: pinned LibreOffice `i18nlangtag/source/languagetag/languagetag.cxx`,
+`LanguageTagImpl::cacheSimpleLSCV`, `getRegionFromLangtag`, `isIsoLocale`,
+`LanguageTag::registerImpl` and `getKnowns`. The simple cache stores country but
+discards the separately extracted numeric region; without an external parser
+owner, getRegionFromLangtag returns that country cache. In a fresh registry,
+the first string-origin es-419 is known without external parsing, then passes
+the short ISO predicate with empty country. Its Locale becomes (es,"","") and
+its suggested primary ID is10. If getKnowns first constructs the actual numeric
+language owners, the ID22538 owner keeps meIsIsoLocale=NO from its qlt conversion;
+the later es-419 string shares that owner and returns (qlt,"",es-419),ID22538.
+The existing upstream QA sequence asserts the latter result after earlier
+initialization. Preserve both source paths and the real registry side effects;
+do not prime registries artificially or make the cache retain numeric regions.
+Evidence: source inspection and isolated managed normal-owner tests,not an
+executed native oracle or a demonstrated document corruption. Task197.
